Stop retrying evidence callbacks the CRM has permanently refused.  A 409 on
the provider_unknown/provider_connected routes means the call already holds a
CONFLICTING terminal truth in the CRM; that state is claimed exactly once and
matching replays return 200, so the 409 can never succeed on a retry.  The
live coordinator retried one such row every ~5 minutes forever (288
"callback retained ... status=409" journal lines per day).

Applies to /usr/local/lib/fanum-voice/fanum_pbx_coordinator.py on the PBX.

  before: 2edfb84f12487fcd0a1b7d23c161ec829ea431b164be756b208fbddc05516a15
  after:  c81d7b047b49b69e9dbe2430793f5f27eea13dff3254e2cfcea15ee09f25f681

The `before` digest is the dial-diagnostics build
(coordinator-dial-diagnostics.patch), live on the PBX since 2026-08-26 — the
owner deployed it while this patch was being prepared, so the owner's next
single deploy takes live straight to the `after` digest with just the
tombstone (a three-block diff).  Rolled forward together with this patch
(same PR): PAYLOAD_DIGESTS in scripts/pbx/fanum-pbx-stage (coordinator line),
EXPECTED_COORDINATOR_SHA256 inside the wrapper
(cutover-wrapper-terminal-conflict-pin.patch), EXPECTED_PBX_WRAPPER_SHA256 in
.github/workflows/set-voice-provider-registry-cutover.yml and
src/__tests__/voice-provider-registry-cutover-workflow.test.ts.

The tombstone is deliberately narrow and fail-closed:

  - only the two evidence routes; ai_result/human_lifecycle 409s keep the
    existing retry behavior until their conflict semantics get their own
    review;
  - only when the response body is byte-for-byte the CRM's own verdict
    {"success":false,"analysisStatus":"conflict"} (route.ts
    conflictingTerminalResult, the sole 409 source on that path); an
    unreadable, empty, or extended body stays retryable;
  - the outbox row is never deleted: delivered_at stops the retry loop while
    last_error_type='terminal_conflict' and last_http_status=409 retain the
    verdict (mark_delivered clears those columns, so tombstones stay
    distinguishable from accepted deliveries);
  - attempts is incremented like mark_delivered does, keeping the
    "attempts = HTTP sends" invariant (deliberate deviation from the reviewed
    design note, recorded here);
  - the payload-hash guard makes the settle race-safe: a concurrent settle or
    a changed payload leaves the row alone and nothing is logged.

Verified offline (no calls placed): station bundle suite keeps an identical
failure fingerprint before/after the change; the updated contract suite adds
six tombstone tests (exact-body tombstone with full audit row, raised-vs-
returned HTTPError paths, fail-closed non-exact bodies, non-evidence routes
untouched, hash-guarded single settle); test_candidate_payload.py still
passes.  The stuck live row settles itself on the first due drain tick after
deploy — no manual sqlite surgery.

